    /**
     * @description The request was refused before anything was priced. `errorCode` is `RequestValidationError` when the body or query failed schema validation, which on `POST /margin/quote` includes sending no action key or more than one, an `open` without a `marketId` that is 0x-prefixed 32-byte hex, a wallet block or `slippageTolerance` on a key that forbids it, a `leverageTarget` at or below 1, an `autoSlippage` or a missing `swapConfig.slippageTolerance`, a `slippageTolerance` or `swapConfig.slippageTolerance` above 5, an `amount` that is zero, has leading zeros or exceeds 2^128 - 1, and a `positionId` with leading zeros or above 2^256 - 1; it is `BadRequest` when the request parsed but the margin domain refused it, with the margin code in `detail`, optionally followed by `: ` and a corrective hint.
     *
     *     On `POST /margin/quote` the codes are: `MARGIN_MARKET_NOT_SUPPORTED`, the chain has no margin configuration (or no v4 quoter), or the position's venue is not configured (a market the service does not serve is not this code: it is a 422 `MARGIN_MARKET_NOT_FOUND` on `open` and `MARGIN_POSITION_NOT_FOUND` on the manage keys); `MARGIN_MARKET_MISMATCH`, on `open`, the market `open.marketId` names is not the request's pair on the side `direction` puts it: on a `LONG` its collateral must be `exposureToken` and its debt `counterToken`, on a `SHORT` the reverse; `MARGIN_MIRRORED_READING`, on `open`, `direction` reads the market in a way `GET /margin/markets` does not list it: a USD stablecoin as the exposure against a volatile token (a `SHORT` of USDT against WBTC is the WBTC long, a `LONG` of USDC against WETH the WETH short), or the `SHORT` of a stablecoin against a stablecoin; against a volatile token send the listed row instead, the volatile token as `exposureToken` and the direction flipped, and a stablecoin against a stablecoin is served only as the `LONG` of its collateral; `MARGIN_INTENT_MISMATCH`, the action key contradicts the numbers. A leverage target on the wrong side of the position's current leverage names the key to send instead on its leverage axis only (`MARGIN_INTENT_MISMATCH: decreaseLeverage` for an `increaseLeverage` aimed below current leverage, and likewise for the composites), a withdrawal of every last unit of collateral from a position that still owes debt, or a withdraw composite taking out all of the equity, names `close`, and a target that moves nothing, or an `open` whose target buys no collateral at all, carries no suffix; `MARGIN_POSITION_NOT_FOUND`, no live position with that `positionId` for this `swapper` on this market, or the account holds collateral on more than one venue's market for the pair and neither debt nor the owner's stored `ACTIVE` position settles which one is the position (anyone can supply collateral to an account but only the account can borrow, so a single market carrying debt is served first, then the single one the stored position names, a stored position recording more collateral than its market now holds naming none); `MARGIN_FUNDING_SWAP_UNSUPPORTED`, `walletChainId` differs from `positionChainId` on a pay-out key, or a pay-out key (`close`, `withdrawEquity` and the withdraw composites) named a `walletToken` other than the position's collateral, with the suffix `pays out in <collateral address>` naming the token to send as `walletToken` instead; `MARGIN_SLIPPAGE_TOLERANCE_REQUIRED`, a leg that swaps reached pricing without an explicit tolerance, a backstop behind the schema, which requires both; `MARGIN_DUST_DEBT`, on the leverage-target keys, the decrease would leave the position owing more than zero but under 10,000 raw units of its debt token, too little for any venue mark to read; raise `leverageTarget`, or `close`; `MARGIN_LEVERAGE_EXCEEDS_MAX` on `open` only, the market `open.marketId` names has a buffered leverage ceiling below `leverageTarget`, so lowering it is the fix (a market lending nothing against the collateral is a 422 `MARGIN_NO_ELIGIBLE_VENUE` instead, since no target is servable) (on the manage keys the same code is a 422, because the position's own state decides it).
     *
     *     On `GET /margin/markets` the codes are: `MARGIN_MARKET_NOT_SUPPORTED`, the chain has no margin configuration; `MARGIN_INVALID_CURSOR`, a `cursor` that does not decode, refused rather than restarting at page one. An unrecognised `venues` value is a `RequestValidationError`.
     *
     *     On `GET /margin/positions` the codes are: `MARGIN_MARKET_NOT_SUPPORTED`, the chain has no margin configuration; `MARGIN_INVALID_CURSOR`, a `cursor` that is base64 but does not decode. `statuses` that mix `ACTIVE` with a finished status, name a status twice, are empty or fall outside the enum, and the retired `status` parameter, are a `RequestValidationError`.
     *
     *     On `GET /margin/assets` the code is `MARGIN_MARKET_NOT_SUPPORTED`, the chain has no margin configuration. A missing or non-numeric `chainId`, or any query key besides `chainId`, is a `RequestValidationError`.
     */
